{"text": "June", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">June</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">june</i>, re-Latinised variants of earlier Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">Juyn</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">juyng</i>, from Old French <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">juing</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">juin</i>, from Latin <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">i\u016bnius</i>, the month of the goddess <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">Iuno</i> (\u201cJuno\u201d), perhaps from Proto-Indo-European <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ine-pro\">*h\u2082y\u00e9wH\u014d</i>, from Proto-Indo-European <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ine-pro\">*h\u2082\u00f3yu</i> (\u201cvital force, youthful vigor\u201d).\n</p>", "pos": []}, {"etymologyHTML": "<p>Short for <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">junior</i>.\n</p>", "pos": []}], "pronunciation": [["Received Pronunciation", "/d\u0361\u0292u\u02d0n/"], ["General American", "/d\u0361\u0292un/"]]}